From 96c8c3e5ff82587320f48b8440ab50a102827308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:17:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Run on FreeBSD with unfs3 as the NFS server

NFS Ganesha has no FreeBSD port, and FreeBSD's kernel nfsd can only run in
a privileged pod (jail allow.nfsd), while this provisioner's pod is not
privileged. On FreeBSD the provisioner's own server (run-server, the
default) is unfs3, a user-space NFSv3 server:

- server: Setup starts rpcbind and creates the exports file; Run runs
  unfsd in the foreground (MOUNT on 20048, NFS on 2049) with its output in
  the log file.
- volume: the run-server exporter writes unfs3 export lines (no fsid
  option and no '*' host in unfs3; the export ID goes in a comment, where
  the restart recovery finds it) and makes unfsd reread them with SIGHUP.
  The D-Bus Ganesha exporter moves to a !freebsd file.

NFSv3 only: unfs3 has no NFSv4.
